<code>assert \old(this.containsKey(key)) => !this.containsKey(key) && !this.containsValue(\old(this.get(key)));</code>

This assertion ensures that if the key was present in the map before the removal, it is no longer present in the map, and the value associated with that key is also no longer in the map. Note that `containsValue` checks for the presence of any key mapping to the given value, which indirectly ensures that the specific value associated with the removed key is no longer in the map.--------------------<code>assert \old(this.containsKey(key)) => !this.containsKey(key) && !this.containsValue(\old(this.get(key)));</code>

This assert statement checks that if the key was present in the map before the removal (`\old(this.containsKey(key))`), then after the removal, the key is no longer in the map (`!this.containsKey(key)`) and the value that was associated with the key is no longer in the map (`!this.containsValue(\old(this.get(key)))`).--------------------<code>assert \old(this.containsKey(key)) => !this.containsKey(key) && !this.containsValue(\old(this.get(key)));</code>

This assert statement checks that if the key was present in the map before the removal (`\old(this.containsKey(key))`), then after the removal, the key is no longer in the map (`!this.containsKey(key)`) and the value that was associated with the key is no longer in the map (`!this.containsValue(\old(this.get(key)))`).--------------------